From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:46:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 443/488] [DS4.1] Disk Engram IDs hashed in place, image tokens
 found in the ids

The TileLang hash and gate take the step's token ids and find the image
sentinel themselves: no mask kernels before them. The model keeps the
step's row IDs layer-major; each disk Engram layer reads its own plane
and the hash's live token count, so staging copies nothing.
